+// A text painted: its cells in `rgb` at `k` (and ×`level(i, j)`, per cell,
+// where they are laid before any offset), blocking `a` behind them. A
+// fractional `dx` or `dy` moves it as light leaning. A cell at no level is
+// not written. Answers where it went: its left edge and last column by its
+// advance (so `right` is its last column), its rows from its capitals' tops
+// to its lowest lit row, and its cells as laid
