+  // the jump cut at 720 takes all four lines)
+  wed: { from: 560, to: 720, dim: [560, 600], blink: 30, blinkOn: 16, wake: 600, wakeStep: 2, lines: [600, 600, 620, 640] },
+  // 4b · later, the same lock screen: the cut lands as the notification is
+  // already rising, its spring started two frames before
+  later: { from: 720, to: 800, spring: 718, rowsIn: 4 },
+  // 5 · her note. She reads; options, and the ask is there (the menu
+  // between them is cut: its last row was the ask's own title and its key,
+  // `let it go` three times in half a second); a half press that never
+  // commits, held, let go; stillness; keep it. A page a press opens is the
+  // LCD's own four frames of its rows coming on where they are, never a
+  // sheet rising (the notification's rise is the film's one arrival from
+  // below, the chat's scroll its one scroll). Her note reads for two
+  // seconds, the film's title line given the time; the ask, a dialog, is
+  // what is quick (read for a second and a little at 64 frames, the line
