+}
+
+// The limbo, from the photograph's masks, in the panel's cells. Which
+// cells are the bouquet's (`soft`): the photograph's red over its green
+// leaves holes in the heads where the dark leaves come up between them,
+// and at a phone's size two of them were a face's eyes; so the mask is
+// closed first (grown and shrunk again by CLOSE cells), any hole left in
+// it that the panel's edge cannot reach is filled, and any cell still out
+// of it with HOLE of its 7 × 7 round it in it is let in, and the cells so
+// let in (`leaf`) are the bouquet's dark folds and never its petals. Its
+// edge is left to the cells' own hashes over its last three cells, so it
+// is ragged as a dither is, never a cut-out, and none of it on or under
+// `it’s mutual`'s line. For each head cell its step by how pink it is
+// among the heads (`q`, its hash dithering it), and the frame it takes the
+// rose (the pinkest first, over S.nine.roseSpread); the hands' cells; each
+// cell's level in the print (`lv`, the photograph's own order: the sky
+// light, the heads at HEAD by `q`, the stems, the leaves and the hands
+// DARK) and how much of the sky it is; and the heads' middle and the
+// middles of their thirds, left to right, on the frame (px)
+const CLOSE = 3
+const HOLE = 0.6
+const ROSY_R = 2
+let BOUQUET = null
